{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21526190",
      "title": "Global vs Local Components",
      "lectureOrder": 112,
      "videoOrder": 95,
      "sourceHash": "00d921d59a26e72d25f8e7ee4a267413279f8b110aba7104020ad0048d003967",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 4.57,
          "en": "Let's start with Component Registration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.57,
          "end": 7.01,
          "en": "We are registering our components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.01,
          "end": 9.84,
          "en": "with the component method on our App.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.84,
          "end": 14.1,
          "en": "And that's how we did it in all the past modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.1,
          "end": 18.27,
          "en": "Now, there is nothing wrong with this approach per se.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.27,
          "end": 20.74,
          "en": "But it's also not always the best way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.74,
          "end": 22.36,
          "en": "of registering components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.36,
          "end": 25.62,
          "en": "Because it turns out there is an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.62,
          "end": 28.39,
          "en": "Now, when we register components like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.39,
          "end": 31.26,
          "en": "with the component method on our App,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.26,
          "end": 34.93,
          "en": "then we are registering those components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.93,
          "end": 38.86,
          "en": "as so called Global Components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.86,
          "end": 42.08,
          "en": "That means they're available globally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.08,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "in this entire Vue App.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 46.6,
          "en": "So we can use these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.6,
          "end": 51.6,
          "en": "as custom HTML elements anywhere in this App.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.7,
          "end": 56.7,
          "en": "In the App.Vue file, but also in any of our components here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.23,
          "end": 61.54,
          "en": "So they're simply available anywhere in this Route App.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.54,
          "end": 63.14,
          "en": "This is of course very useful,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.14,
          "end": 66.15,
          "en": "because it means we can use these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 66.15,
          "end": 68.14,
          "en": "as custom elements anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.14,
          "end": 71.43,
          "en": "And we don't have to think about where to use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.43,
          "end": 74.39,
          "en": "But it also has one potential downside.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.39,
          "end": 77.53,
          "en": "These components, of course, all contain some code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.53,
          "end": 80.73,
          "en": "Now, of course, here, they're all fairly simple components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.73,
          "end": 83.19,
          "en": "But still, it's a little bit of template code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.19,
          "end": 85.2,
          "en": "a little bit of scripting code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.2,
          "end": 87.68,
          "en": "Now, this code, of course grows,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.68,
          "end": 89.5,
          "en": "the bigger our application becomes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.5,
          "end": 92.49000000000001,
          "en": "The more components we have, the more code packages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.49000000000001,
          "end": 93.93,
          "en": "we have, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.93,
          "end": 97.09,
          "en": "And if you're registering them all globally,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.09,
          "end": 101.72999999999999,
          "en": "that in the end means Vue needs to load them all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.72999999999999,
          "end": 104.27000000000001,
          "en": "when the application is loaded initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.27000000000001,
          "end": 106.71000000000001,
          "en": "So the browser needs to download the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.71000000000001,
          "end": 108.963,
          "en": "for all those components initially.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.33,
          "end": 112.11,
          "en": "This is absolutely no problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112.11,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "for our basic application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 117.31,
          "en": "but for bigger applications, that could be a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.31,
          "end": 121.26,
          "en": "In addition, if you register everything globally here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.26,
          "end": 123.87,
          "en": "this can be a very long list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.87,
          "end": 126.05,
          "en": "If you have a application with, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.05,
          "end": 129.55,
          "en": "hundreds of components, this would be a super long list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 129.55,
          "end": 131.98,
          "en": "And it would not be obvious where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.98,
          "end": 133.71,
          "en": "those components are getting used.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 133.71,
          "end": 135.99,
          "en": "If all these components are meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.99,
          "end": 138.95,
          "en": "to be used in multiple places, or if maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.95,
          "end": 142.393,
          "en": "some of these components are only used in a few places.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.57999999999998,
          "end": 145.32,
          "en": "For example, TheHeader.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.32,
          "end": 148.26,
          "en": "This component is really only used once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.26,
          "end": 152.52,
          "en": "It's used here in App.Vue, the same for UserInfo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 152.52,
          "end": 154.92000000000002,
          "en": "These are components which are just getting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 154.92000000000002,
          "end": 159.82999999999998,
          "en": "used once and registering them globally, therefore works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.82999999999998,
          "end": 162.103,
          "en": "But there's a bit redundant, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 163.4,
          "end": 165.86,
          "en": "We're just having these components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 165.86,
          "end": 168.06,
          "en": "so that we can outsource our code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 170.64,
          "en": "and keep our App.Vue file lean,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 170.64,
          "end": 172.64,
          "en": "because that's the idea behind components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 172.64,
          "end": 175.4,
          "en": "We wanna build complex user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.4,
          "end": 177.853,
          "en": "by combining multiple building blocks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 181.27,
          "en": "That's why we also have another way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 181.27,
          "end": 183.34,
          "en": "of registering components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 183.34,
          "end": 185.86,
          "en": "Despite registering them globally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 185.86,
          "end": 188.4,
          "en": "with this component method on our App,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 191.84,
          "en": "we can also register them locally in the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 191.84,
          "end": 193.57,
          "en": "where we plan on using them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.57,
          "end": 195.62,
          "en": "So for example, with TheHeader,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 195.62,
          "end": 199.86,
          "en": "we could remove this component registration in main.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 199.86,
          "end": 202.54,
          "en": "and remove this import here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 202.54,
          "end": 205.63,
          "en": "And instead go to our App.Vue file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 205.63,
          "end": 207.97,
          "en": "which is where we plan on using this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 207.97,
          "end": 210.23,
          "en": "And then here in the script section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 210.23,
          "end": 215.23,
          "en": "we can import TheHeader from components TheHeader.Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.17000000000002,
          "end": 222.55,
          "en": "And now we can also register this component locally",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 222.55,
          "end": 226.36,
          "en": "in this App component or in this App object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.36,
          "end": 228.683,
          "en": "in this App options object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.19,
          "end": 232.91,
          "en": "We do this by adding a new property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 232.91,
          "end": 235.81,
          "en": "next to data methods computed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.81,
          "end": 237.99,
          "en": "and all the other properties you learned about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 237.99,
          "end": 241.43,
          "en": "and that would be the components property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 241.43,
          "end": 244.023,
          "en": "which we haven't seen before, but here it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.96,
          "end": 248.93,
          "en": "And we can now tell Vue, which components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.93,
          "end": 252.74,
          "en": "may be used in the template of this App here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.74,
          "end": 254.62,
          "en": "or of this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.62,
          "end": 256.92,
          "en": "And the components registered here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 256.92,
          "end": 259.64,
          "en": "are then really only usable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.64,
          "end": 262,
          "en": "not in any other child components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262,
          "end": 264.53,
          "en": "not anywhere else in our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.53,
          "end": 268.543,
          "en": "just here in this file, in this .Vue file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 270.11,
          "end": 272.09000000000003,
          "en": "Now components wants an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 272.09000000000003,
          "end": 274.68,
          "en": "and then we need a key-value pair,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 274.68,
          "end": 278.40999999999997,
          "en": "where the key is our custom HTML element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 278.40999999999997,
          "end": 282.14,
          "en": "So TheHeader for example, the tag we wanna use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 282.14,
          "end": 283.77,
          "en": "for this element, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 283.77,
          "end": 286.77,
          "en": "and then the value is the imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 286.77,
          "end": 289.263,
          "en": "component config object, we're pointing at.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 290.741,
          "end": 294.98,
          "en": "And If I do that, and Save this, this still all works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 294.98,
          "end": 298.25,
          "en": "But now TheHeader is registered locally.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.25,
          "end": 300.56,
          "en": "And you can actually also write this differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 300.56,
          "end": 303.07,
          "en": "This is perfectly fine, but you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 303.07,
          "end": 307.51,
          "en": "also use TheHeader like this as a key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.51,
          "end": 310.37,
          "en": "as a property name and you will still be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 310.37,
          "end": 313.21,
          "en": "to use it like this in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 313.21,
          "end": 315.93,
          "en": "Vue automatically translates this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 315.93,
          "end": 319.94,
          "en": "so that you can use the-header in your template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 319.94,
          "end": 324.94,
          "en": "or in case you prefer it, TheHeader like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 324.94,
          "end": 326.1,
          "en": "And then you can also write it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 326.1,
          "end": 328.683,
          "en": "as a self-closing element if you want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 329.54,
          "end": 332.7,
          "en": "This self-closing tag is not supported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.7,
          "end": 335.26,
          "en": "if you write it with a dash in between,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 335.26,
          "end": 337.87,
          "en": "then this self-closing tag will not work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.87,
          "end": 340.753,
          "en": "if you write it in this PascallCase it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 341.82,
          "end": 344.82,
          "en": "So this is then up to you which style you prefer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 344.82,
          "end": 347.37,
          "en": "I will stick to the-header because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 347.37,
          "end": 349.48,
          "en": "that's the style I've been using before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 349.48,
          "end": 352.453,
          "en": "but you could now also use this PascalCase style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 353.44,
          "end": 356.88,
          "en": "When you register it like this both is possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 356.88,
          "end": 358.85,
          "en": "And then you can shorten this even more,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 358.85,
          "end": 361.42,
          "en": "you can remove this key here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 361.42,
          "end": 364.22,
          "en": "and just pass TheHeader like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 364.22,
          "end": 367.5,
          "en": "because there is a modern JavaScript syntax feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 367.5,
          "end": 369.85,
          "en": "which is supported in this project setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 369.85,
          "end": 373.29,
          "en": "where if you just provide a single value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 373.29,
          "end": 378.29,
          "en": "in an object, this is automatically expanded to this syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 378.78,
          "end": 382.02,
          "en": "So that's simply key and value variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 382.02,
          "end": 384.633,
          "en": "or value constant have the same name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 385.94,
          "end": 388.387,
          "en": "So you can then just write TheHeader",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 388.387,
          "end": 391.457,
          "en": "and this will register this TheHeader component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 391.457,
          "end": 394.509,
          "en": "under the TheHeader identifier, and you can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 394.509,
          "end": 397.32,
          "en": "then use the-header like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 397.32,
          "end": 401.22,
          "en": "or as I explained before, use this PascalCase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 401.22,
          "end": 402.17,
          "en": "if you prefer that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 403.40999999999997,
          "end": 406.163,
          "en": "That if we Save that would also work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 407.07,
          "end": 410.40999999999997,
          "en": "So this is how you can write your components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
